\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Parametric sweep of the two speed-sensitive indicators across the engine-speed range 6\,000--12\,000~rpm for the AP 1.8 head at fixed geometry. The dynamic-ratio criterion is $R\geq 1.20$ and the surge-ratio rule-of-thumb is $f_{n}/f_{\mathrm  {cam}}\geq 4$. The intersection of the two pass criteria defines an analytical safe-operation envelope of approximately 6\,000--10\,500~rpm for the baseline configuration; barriers transition to at-risk above this band and the loss-of-contact boundary ($R\to 1$) is crossed near 11\,500~rpm.}}{10}{table.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tbl:rpm-sweep}{{6}{10}{Parametric sweep of the two speed-sensitive indicators across the engine-speed range 6\,000--12\,000~rpm for the AP 1.8 head at fixed geometry. The dynamic-ratio criterion is $R\geq 1.20$ and the surge-ratio rule-of-thumb is $f_{n}/f_{\mathrm {cam}}\geq 4$. The intersection of the two pass criteria defines an analytical safe-operation envelope of approximately 6\,000--10\,500~rpm for the baseline configuration; barriers transition to at-risk above this band and the loss-of-contact boundary ($R\to 1$) is crossed near 11\,500~rpm}{table.6}{}}
